---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const allProjects = await getCollection('projects');
const triptych = allProjects
  .filter(p => p.data.series === 'Organic Memory (Triptych)')
  .sort((a, b) => (a.data.seriesOrder ?? 0) - (b.data.seriesOrder ?? 0));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Organic Memory (Triptych) | Conscious Form"
  description="Three interactive sonic sculptures that make up Organic Memory (Triptych), the composition at the center of my PhD dissertation."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">

    <a href="/projects" class="text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors mb-4 inline-block">
      ← Back to Projects
    </a>

    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">
        Dissertation Work · Triptych
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Organic Memory</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-neutral-400 mb-2">(Triptych)</p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose prose-invert max-w-none mb-16">
      <p><em>Organic Memory (Triptych)</em> is a composition for three interactive sonic sculptures, and the center of my PhD dissertation. Each instrument reads one material and keeps that material's tempo: <em>Buffalo Soldier</em> listens to soil and rock at a geological tempo (EARTH), <em>Did Sun Ra Fear Cryosleep?</em> to dissolving water at a chemical one (WATER), and <em>Don't Play with My Hair</em> to the structure of hair at a human one (FLESH). A rhythmic cell from the closing phrase of <em>When Johnny Comes Marching Home</em> appears in all three, stretched or compressed to each tempo, over a low drone shared by every movement. I call the method behind the instruments <em>speculocultural technopoiesis</em>: modifying a specific tool under a specific cultural epistemology, with that epistemology as the stated standard of success.</p>
    </section>

    {/* The three pieces */}
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-8">The Three Pieces</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        {triptych.map(project => (
          <a
            href={`/projects/${project.slug}`}
            class="group flex gap-6 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-6 hover:border-neutral-600 transition-colors"
          >
            {project.data.thumbnail ? (
              <img
                src={project.data.thumbnail}
                alt={project.data.title}
                class="w-40 h-28 object-cover rounded flex-shrink-0"
              />
            ) : (
              <div class="w-40 h-28 bg-neutral-800 rounded flex-shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center">
                <span class="text-neutral-600 text-xs">No image</span>
              </div>
            )}
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 mb-1">Part {project.data.seriesOrder}</p>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold group-hover:text-white mb-2 transition-colors">
                {project.data.title}
              </h3>
              <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">{project.data.description}</p>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-3">
                {project.data.tags.map(tag => (
                  <span class="text-xs bg-neutral-800 px-2 py-1 rounded">{tag}</span>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>
</BaseLayout>
